<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 232 0 R
/E ( The shipping industry is the backbone of global trade, moving goods across oceans every day. A key factor in ship operations is speed, which influences fuel use, costs, and timely deliveries. Environmental conditions like wind, waves, and currents can affect how vessels move, making it important to understand their impact. Modern sensors, GPS, and tracking systems allow us to collect vast amounts of data, and machine learning can help uncover patterns that improve predictions of vessel speed and enable real-time monitoring, providing operators with useful insights to maintain efficiency and safety.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
